# Cloudflare Workers static-asset headers. Workers Static Assets serves files
# from .open-next/assets BEFORE the Worker runs, and these rules apply ONLY to
# those asset responses — never to Worker-rendered ones (pages, API routes,
# prerendered HTML served through the incremental cache), which get their
# headers from next.config.ts headers(). So nothing here can clobber the HTML
# Content-Security-Policy, and the /* block deliberately carries NO CSP.
# Values mirror next.config.ts SECURITY_HEADERS (asserted in
# tests/static-headers.test.ts). HSTS is left to the Cloudflare edge setting.
#
# Next's build output under /_next/static/ is content-hashed: a changed file
# gets a new name, so a cached copy can never go stale. Without this rule
# Workers serves every asset with `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, so each page
# view re-validates the render-blocking CSS, every JS chunk, font and media file.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off

# An SVG opened directly is a document that could run script. Every SVG here is
# owner-authored and shown via <img> (where CSP is moot), but lock the document
# form down anyway: no script, no external fetches, inline presentation only.
/*.svg
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; frame-ancestors 'none'
